# SPDX-License-Identifier: MPL-2.0
# Adjustfile — Drift-tolerance contract for boj-server-cartridges
# Author: Jonathan D.A. Jewell <j.d.a.jewell@open.ac.uk>
#
# Paired runner: adjust.ncl
# Verb:          adjust
#
# Cumulative-drift catchment: tolerance bands + corrective actions.
# Authority: advisory (Yard) — continue-with-warnings; auto_fix where deterministic.
# Run with: adjust check
# Fix with: adjust fix (applies deterministic patches; advisory otherwise)
#
# Rewritten 2026-08-07. The previous version was rsr-template-repo's own
# Adjustfile and tracked template-distribution drift, which is not a thing
# that happens here.

[metadata]
project = "boj-server-cartridges"
version = "0.2.0"
last-updated = "2026-08-07"

@abstract:
Drift tolerances and corrective actions for boj-server-cartridges. Unlike
MUST (hard gate), ADJUST tracks cumulative drift against tolerance bands and
proposes corrective actions. Advisory — it warns and trends, it does not
block.

The dominant drift risk in this repository is REPETITION. 142 cartridges
minted from one template means one template defect becomes 142, and one
vendored file becomes 116 copies that nothing compares. Every band below is
calibrated to that.
@end

## Vendored-Copy Drift

### cartridge-shim-drift
- description: Every vendored cartridge_shim.zig should be byte-identical to the minting template's
- tolerance: 0 copies differing from cartridges/templates/gossamer-mcp/ffi/cartridge_shim.zig
- measured: 1 of 116 differs (cartridges/domains/gaming/npc-mcp/ffi/cartridge_shim.zig), measured 2026-08-07 on commit 972cf0e
- probe: canon=$(sha256sum cartridges/templates/gossamer-mcp/ffi/cartridge_shim.zig | awk '{print $1}'); find cartridges -name cartridge_shim.zig -exec sha256sum {} \; | grep -cv "^$canon"
- corrective: Determine whether npc-mcp's divergence is intentional. If not, copy the template bytes over it. If it is, the divergence needs a recorded reason, because nothing else in the tree explains it.
- severity: advisory
- notes: Open PR #109 proposes tools/sync_cartridge_shim.sh --check and a shim-drift CI job, which would move this from a measured band to an enforced one.

### shim-coverage
- description: Every ffi/ with a build.zig should carry a shim beside it
- tolerance: 0 exceptions
- measured: 2 exceptions — cartridges/domains/languages/007-mcp/ffi and cartridges/domains/knowledge/librarian-mcp/ffi each have build.zig with no cartridge_shim.zig. A third cartridge, orchestrator-lsp-mcp, keeps its build graph at ffi/zig/build.zig and has no shim at all.
- probe: for f in $(find cartridges -path '*/ffi/build.zig'); do d=$(dirname "$f"); test -f "$d/cartridge_shim.zig" || echo "$d"; done
- corrective: Either add the shim or record the exception in 0-AI-MANIFEST.a2ml's invariant list. The manifest now records them rather than asserting a false universal.
- severity: advisory

## Toolchain Drift

### zig-pin-agreement
- description: One zig version across .tool-versions and every workflow that installs zig
- tolerance: exact agreement
- measured: DISAGREES — .tool-versions says 0.15.1, .github/workflows/zig-test.yml installs 0.15.2 (2026-08-07)
- probe: awk '/^zig /{print $2}' .tool-versions; grep -oE 'version: [0-9]+\.[0-9]+\.[0-9]+' .github/workflows/zig-test.yml
- corrective: Pick one. Open PR #109 moves both to 0.16.0.
- severity: advisory

### schema-pin-agreement
- description: The upstream commit named in 0-AI-MANIFEST.a2ml should match the one in schemas/PINNED-SHA
- tolerance: exact agreement
- measured: DISAGREES — the manifest's upstream.schema_canonical_commit and PINNED-SHA's canonical_commit name different commits (2026-08-07)
- probe: grep 'schema_canonical_commit' 0-AI-MANIFEST.a2ml; grep 'canonical_commit' schemas/PINNED-SHA
- corrective: schemas/PINNED-SHA is the operative record — CI verifies against it. Update the manifest to match it, or explain in the manifest why the two differ.
- severity: advisory

## Completeness Drift

### abi-dirs-without-proofs
- description: Every abi/ directory should contain at least one Idris2 proof
- tolerance: 0 empty abi/ dirs
- measured: 18 of 126 abi/ dirs contain no .idr file at all (2026-08-07; 114 .idr files are unevenly distributed across the remaining 108)
- probe: for d in $(find cartridges -type d -name abi); do test -n "$(find "$d" -name '*.idr' -print -quit)" || echo "$d"; done
- corrective: Write the proof, or remove the empty directory so the count stops implying coverage that is not there.
- severity: advisory
- notes: scripts/typecheck-proofs.sh has a vacuous-pass guard for the whole run, but an individually empty abi/ still passes silently.

### cartridges-without-readmes
- description: Every cartridge directory should have a README.adoc
- tolerance: 0 missing
- measured: 11 of 142 cartridge directories have no README.adoc (2026-08-07)
- probe: for f in $(find cartridges -name cartridge.json); do d=$(dirname "$f"); test -f "$d/README.adoc" || echo "$d"; done
- corrective: Write the README, or generate a stub from cartridge.json.
- severity: advisory

## Documentation Drift

### count-staleness
- description: Numbers asserted in docs should match a fresh recount
- tolerance: 0 stale counts
- measured: README.adoc still says "139 manifests, 139 passing, 0 failing"; the true figure is 142/142/0 (2026-08-07)
- probe: cd tools/validate-cartridges && deno task audit | grep 'Manifests:'
- corrective: Recount and update. Never carry a number forward from another artefact.
- severity: advisory
- notes: 0-AI-MANIFEST.a2ml's baseline was corrected 2026-08-07; README.adoc was left for a separate change so the two are not confused with one another.

### adoc-not-md
- description: General prose docs should be AsciiDoc; .md is reserved for the files GitHub special-cases by name
- tolerance: 0 general .md under docs/
- measured: 1 — docs/echo-types-integration-audit-2026-06-01.md (2026-08-07)
- probe: find docs -name '*.md'
- corrective: Convert to .adoc, or accept it and record the exception.
- severity: advisory

### dangling-path-references
- description: No machine-readable artefact should cite a path that does not resolve
- tolerance: 0 dangling references
- measured: 0 within .machine_readable/ as of 2026-08-07. One remains OUTSIDE it: .claude/CLAUDE.md still states that "Cartridge adapter/ dirs keep a SIDELINED-*.v.adoc note", and no such file exists anywhere in this repository or its history.
- probe: grep -rn 'SIDELINED' .claude/CLAUDE.md
- corrective: Correct that sentence in .claude/CLAUDE.md. Left unedited by the docs/machine-readable-repair branch on purpose — CLAUDE.md is operator configuration, not a machine-readable artefact, so it is reported rather than changed.
- severity: advisory

## Structural Drift

### contractile-sync
- description: All contractiles should have matching a2ml and ncl implementations
- tolerance: Every .a2ml has a corresponding .ncl runner
- measured: 0 of 6 have one — no .ncl files exist in this repository at all
- probe: find .machine_readable/contractiles -name '*.ncl'
- corrective: Generate the runners, or stop naming a "paired runner" in each contractile header. Today every contractile claims a runner that does not exist.
- severity: advisory

### justfile-hardlink
- description: The RSR convention hardlinks the root Justfile to .machine_readable/contractiles/Justfile
- tolerance: same inode
- measured: DIFFERENT inodes and different content — .machine_readable/contractiles/Justfile is still rsr-template-repo's template Justfile (project := "rsr-template-repo"), not a link to this repo's
- probe: stat -c '%i %n' Justfile .machine_readable/contractiles/Justfile
- corrective: Decide whether the contractiles Justfile is meant to be a link or an independent template copy, then make it one of those two things. Out of scope for the docs/machine-readable-repair branch, which touched only .a2ml files.
- severity: advisory

### no-broken-symlinks
- description: No broken symbolic links
- tolerance: 0
- measured: 0 (2026-08-07)
- probe: find . -path ./.git -prune -o -xtype l -print
- severity: advisory

## Licensing Drift

### spdx-header-consistency
- description: Source and machine-readable files should carry an SPDX-License-Identifier
- tolerance: 0 missing
- corrective: Add the identifier. MOVE an existing one if it is not on line 1 rather than adding a second — a duplicated or shadowing header is worse than a misplaced one.
- severity: advisory
- notes: Not measured on 2026-08-07. Recorded as unmeasured rather than assumed clean.

### license-boundary
- description: Code is MPL-2.0; documentation is CC-BY-SA-4.0; AGPL never
- tolerance: 0 AGPL declarations outside LICENSES/ and outside files that merely name the policy
- measured: 1 real hit — cartridges/domains/gaming/idaptik-admin-mcp/panels/manifest.json declares "spdx": "AGPL-3.0-or-later" (2026-08-07). The other grep hits are this file, Trustfile.a2ml and AGENTIC.a2ml stating the policy itself.
- probe: git grep -n 'AGPL' -- ':!LICENSES' ':!.machine_readable'
- corrective: Establish whether idaptik-admin-mcp's panel manifest is genuinely AGPL upstream or was clobbered by a licence sweep. Do not flip it blind — the estate has previously flattened correctly-AGPL projects with a mass rewrite.
- severity: advisory
